{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Exalted</b> — He is exalted above all praises, that all nations praise Him, which are in seven regions, from the rising of the sun to its setting. And the sign for this: for above the heavens is His glory, which are above all nations. And it is possible that רם (exalted) draws after it [an implied word], as [if it said] ורם על השמים כבודו (and exalted above the heavens is His glory)."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 113, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:39:34.781481411Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}